@@ -6,6 +6,8 @@ description: "Desktop runs the Harness workspace in a native application. This r
 
 English | [中文](README.zh.md)
 
+Portable bundles use `<root>/app/<exe>` beside `<root>/home`. The bundle directory owns each instance and isolates DSH-owned data without changing inherited user or third-party tool environment settings: sessions, configuration, credentials, plugins and dependency runtimes live under `home`, and shared agent configuration under `home/.agents`. Electron user and session data, logs, crash reports, temporary files, update caches and journals live under `data`. External tools retain their original user directories, configuration and caches. Different bundle directories run concurrently; launching the same directory focuses its owner, with directory aliases resolved to the real path. Both the executable and launcher follow this rule. Portable mode neither registers the system `dsh://` protocol nor reads the system login shell to override bundle paths. Explicit workspace paths and external application installation directories remain accessible. Existing system Electron data is not imported automatically; see the [portable directory upgrade guide](../../docs/upgrade-guide/v0.2.1-alpha.2/portable-data/guide.md).
+
 ## Summary
 
 Desktop runs the Harness workspace in a native application. This reference covers application behavior, development and integration; the packaging, Windows signing and publication guides own build and release operations.
